<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="012" project="spaarkeai-compose-r6">
  <metadata>
    <title>Retire ComposeShadowPatchEngine + ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper from the save path</title>
    <phase>1 Render-on-save core</phase>
    <gate>blocked — requires 001 (ADR-049 Path-B amendment merged) + 011 (generalized renderer)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Core BFF save-path change (tags bff/compose) removing the surgical patcher/count-gate; governed by the ADR amendment — FULL per root §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified retirement of a known code path once 010/011 land; sonnet default per §8.5.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <effort-reason>Brownfield removal on a contested surface requiring careful reachability analysis; high per §8.5.</effort-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits Services/Compose save-path wiring — most-contested BFF surface (overlaps spaarkeai-compose-r5/r4.5/r3/r2/r1, spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2, agreements-r1, analysis-hub-r1). Serialize all Compose edits.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001, 011</deps>
    <tags>bff, compose</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Remove ComposeShadowPatchEngine and the ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper count-gate from the SaveAsync path, retaining the surgical engine ONLY for the transitional clean-apply path explicitly permitted by the ADR-049 amendment. Prove by static reachability that no normal save invokes the surgical patcher or the count-gate.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Deep expertise in the Compose save path, reachability analysis, and the ADR-049 Path-B amendment. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>No code path reachable from ComposeService.SaveAsync (for a normal save) invokes ComposeShadowPatchEngine or the ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper count-gate; both types remain in the codebase for the transitional clean-apply path; docxBridge.ts is untouched; the BFF builds green and the NDA-class w14:paraId/count mismatch no longer refuses a save.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec FR-02: the count-gate (ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper.cs:113) and ComposeShadowPatchEngine are removed from the save path once render-on-save (010/011) is in place. The surgical engine is retained only for a transitional clean-apply path the amendment permits — it is NOT deleted. This task finalizes the retirement wiring and proves reachability.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — remove surgical-patch + count-gate invocations from the save path.</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper.cs:113 — the count-gate; ensure it is not reached from a normal SaveAsync (retain the type).</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs — retained ONLY for transitional clean-apply per the amendment; do not delete.</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">ADR-049 Path-B amendment (retains surgical engine only for transitional clean-apply) merged with/before this code.</dependency>
      <dependency task="011" status="pending">Generalized render-from-model renderer in place so the save path no longer needs the surgical patcher.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-049">Scope: retain ComposeShadowPatchEngine ONLY for the transitional clean-apply path named in the task-001 amendment; MUST NOT invoke it (or the count-gate) from a normal save.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: NEVER delete docxBridge.ts and do NOT delete ComposeShadowPatchEngine or ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper types — retire them from the save path only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Scope: keep Services/Compose byte[]-in / projection-out; no Microsoft.Graph above SpeFileStore.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Scope: NO AI-internal types in Services/Compose; consume Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ seams only if needed — no fork.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Scope: engine frozen — no new AI dispatch endpoint.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (Placement Justification, root §10): modify-only of existing Services/Compose — cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md in the PR, verify publish size ≤60 MB (absolute + delta vs task-003 baseline), verify no new HIGH CVE, run /conflict-check before the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Save-path retirement; reachability analysis; transitional clean-apply</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/COMPOSE-READ-REFERENCE-FIDELITY.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Transitional retention" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs">Keep the engine as a retained type for the clean-apply path the amendment permits; only sever its save-path invocation.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare RIGOR LEVEL: FULL, model-tier sonnet, effort high. Confirm 001 merged + 011 in place (gate); run /conflict-check for Services/Compose.</step>
    <step order="1">Enumerate every call site of ComposeShadowPatchEngine + the count-gate reachable from SaveAsync.</step>
    <step order="2">Sever those invocations from the normal save path; retain the types + the transitional clean-apply path.</step>
    <step order="3">Static-verify (grep/reachability) that no normal-save code path reaches the surgical patcher or count-gate.</step>
    <step order="4">Build the BFF; measure publish size vs the task-003 baseline; run dotnet list package --vulnerable.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="6">Document the reachability evidence + placement decision + publish-size delta + any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r6/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the surgical patcher / count-gate turns out to be reachable from a save path that is NOT the transitional clean-apply path the amendment permits, STOP and escalate per root §6.5 rather than silently deleting or force-routing around it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given SaveAsync for a normal save, when statically traced, then no reachable path invokes ComposeShadowPatchEngine or the ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper count-gate.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the codebase after this task, when inspected, then ComposeShadowPatchEngine and ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper types still exist (retained for transitional clean-apply) and docxBridge.ts is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an imported document with a w14:paraId/count mismatch, when saved, then the save is not refused.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no Services/Compose type is deleted and no Microsoft.Graph / AI-internal type is introduced.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size ≤60 MB with absolute + delta reported; no new HIGH CVE; BFF builds green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Critical path 001→010→011→012→013→014. Completes the save-path pivot; 013 then proves no-422 + edits-land + new-version by tests. spec FR-02.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
